00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:50.620
It was called Open
Mind, Open Art.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:53.410
We saw flyers advertising
it in the Student Center.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.420
And we thought it was a
really cool opportunity

00:20:55.420 --> 00:20:58.310
to make art during
our freshman IP,

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:01.040
so we decided to
join that project.

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:04.390
The goal of it was
for 10 student artists

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:09.640
to create their own projects
revolving around the theme

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:11.140
of mental health and wellness.

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:16.420
The project was funded by the
Mind, Head, Heart Initiative.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:20.710
And what we really liked
about this project,

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.990
it was also kind of a
community of people.

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:28.320
By the end of the IP, it
was really collaborative.

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:33.250
And everything was
pretty open ended.

00:21:33.250 --> 00:21:36.160
We had this general theme about
mental health and wellness.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:37.780
But besides that,
everyone could take

00:21:37.780 --> 00:21:40.162
their projects in whichever
direction they wanted to.

00:21:40.162 --> 00:21:42.370
So there were people who
made clay sculptures, people

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:47.050
who made paintings,
someone wrote poetry.

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:50.950
And what we decided to do was
make this fiber arts piece.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:53.590
So we were really interested
in various forms of fiber arts

00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:55.780
in high school, like
knitting, sewing.

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:58.280
So we wanted to kind of
take that a step further.

00:21:58.280 --> 00:22:01.220
So what we basically
did for this piece is

00:22:01.220 --> 00:22:03.760
sewed a bunch of little
pieces of fabric together,

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:10.050
specifically felt, to create
this series of six faces.

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:14.200
And the idea behind this
was kind of for the viewer

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:20.590
to empathize with the faces
that we depicted here.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:24.420
And we also kind of made
this little wordplay.

00:22:24.420 --> 00:22:28.140
The title of this piece
is "Stitched Together."

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:30.250
So that kind of has
this double meaning

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:33.460
because the pieces are
literally stitched together

00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:34.870
out of these pieces of fabric.

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:39.250
But we also kind of wanted
to evoke this feeling

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:42.820
that everyone kind of has either
shared struggles or shared

00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:45.790
experiences and can
relate to each other,

00:22:45.790 --> 00:22:48.060
even if not initially evident.

00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:48.560
So yeah.

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:49.870
That was this experience.

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:51.268
It was overall really fun.

00:22:51.268 --> 00:22:52.810
