00:34:59.260 --> 00:35:01.560
or kind of addressed
it within their art,

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:03.670
I don't know if anybody
has any specific answers.

00:35:03.670 --> 00:35:05.460
But it's something I
think a lot about it

00:35:05.460 --> 00:35:07.690
in terms of the
art world and how

00:35:07.690 --> 00:35:10.920
it's not just kind of affecting
individuals, which is normally

00:35:10.920 --> 00:35:11.950
how crises happen.

00:35:11.950 --> 00:35:14.726
But it should be reflected
across, I think, everyone.

00:35:20.680 --> 00:35:26.450
I think, in a way,
at least in ACT,

00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:29.620
what I'm seeing, for
example, this semester,

00:35:29.620 --> 00:35:37.570
is that a lot of
classes are turning

00:35:37.570 --> 00:35:40.810
their heads towards the
outside and the city

00:35:40.810 --> 00:35:42.400
and out to the experiences.

00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:45.210
And I mean, obviously
for practical reasons.

00:35:45.210 --> 00:35:50.510
But also how do we continue
artistic research, for example,

00:35:50.510 --> 00:35:52.780
which is what ACT does?

00:35:52.780 --> 00:35:59.300
How do we continue artistic
research and knowledge?

00:35:59.300 --> 00:36:01.480
How do we keep on
giving knowledge

00:36:01.480 --> 00:36:04.000
without the facilities?

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:05.860
So this semester is
super interesting.

00:36:05.860 --> 00:36:09.100
If you take a look at the
subjects, most of them

00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:13.780
are either choreographing
things in the city,

00:36:13.780 --> 00:36:19.120
walking, thinking about the
outside, not just the city

00:36:19.120 --> 00:36:21.710
but in general.

00:36:21.710 --> 00:36:24.150
So I think that it
changed, I mean,

00:36:24.150 --> 00:36:27.910
it's a super
positive adaptation.

00:36:27.910 --> 00:36:30.080
It changed very quickly.

00:36:30.080 --> 00:36:35.470
So I think that's one of
the really nice things we

00:36:35.470 --> 00:36:38.770
could get, at least.

00:36:38.770 --> 00:36:39.520
It's nice to hear.

00:36:39.520 --> 00:36:40.020
Yeah.

00:36:40.020 --> 00:36:42.218
You've got to find the
silver linings in everything.

00:36:42.218 --> 00:36:44.608
I see that.

00:36:44.608 --> 00:36:46.060
Anyone else?

00:36:46.060 --> 00:36:46.560
Yeah.

00:36:46.560 --> 00:36:50.830
Something I've noticed is that
I've just gotten more excited

00:36:50.830 --> 00:36:53.890
about making do with what
I have like seeing how

00:36:53.890 --> 00:36:56.445
I can get creative with that.

00:36:56.445 --> 00:36:57.820
Like the pants I
showed, I guess.

00:36:57.820 --> 00:37:02.350
Or just viewing items that I
have already in a new light

00:37:02.350 --> 00:37:05.200
and turning them
into something has,

00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:06.850
instead of going
to buy supplies,

00:37:06.850 --> 00:37:08.650
has influenced my art.

00:37:08.650 --> 00:37:11.240
And I honestly think it's made
it more interesting and more

00:37:11.240 --> 00:37:11.740
fruitful.

00:37:15.687 --> 00:37:18.020
I think I saw someone in the
audience unmute themselves.

00:37:18.020 --> 00:37:19.437
I'm not sure if
you had a question

00:37:19.437 --> 00:37:21.042
or if that was accidental.

00:37:21.042 --> 00:37:23.010
I do have a question actually.

00:37:23.010 --> 00:37:25.620
I wonder how much
everyone's process

00:37:25.620 --> 00:37:31.230
has changed in the context
of maybe your process isn't

00:37:31.230 --> 00:37:32.200
as private anymore.

00:37:32.200 --> 00:37:32.700
Right?

00:37:32.700 --> 00:37:35.820
When you had facilities,
you could go into a space,

00:37:35.820 --> 00:37:39.510
work on your craft, and
decide when to showcase

00:37:39.510 --> 00:37:40.590
what you're working on.

00:37:40.590 --> 00:37:43.380
Whereas now, maybe we're
forced in environments ,

00:37:43.380 --> 00:37:45.990
whether it's outdoors or in
a house with somebody else,

00:37:45.990 --> 00:37:49.980
where you have to go through the
whole process from conception

00:37:49.980 --> 00:37:54.690
to refinement in a
less private setting.

00:37:54.690 --> 00:37:58.710
And I wonder how that's
impacted, if at all,

00:37:58.710 --> 00:38:00.420
people's process and experience.

00:38:07.180 --> 00:38:10.330
I mean, I can speak
a little to that.

00:38:10.330 --> 00:38:16.210
One of the things which we took
a decision in our cohort in ACT

00:38:16.210 --> 00:38:21.130
was that we would
isolate within ourselves.

00:38:21.130 --> 00:38:25.390
So we decided that we would make
sure that we saw each other.

00:38:25.390 --> 00:38:28.960
And we found a way to
quarantine only with each other

00:38:28.960 --> 00:38:30.730
so that we could continue.

00:38:30.730 --> 00:38:34.390
I mean, it was very important
for us to work together.

00:38:34.390 --> 00:38:38.920
And what happened with corona
was that it sort of accelerated

00:38:38.920 --> 00:38:41.920
the process of trying to--

00:38:41.920 --> 00:38:45.130
because at some point,
we only had each other.

00:38:45.130 --> 00:38:47.200
And that really made--

00:38:47.200 --> 00:38:51.610
I mean, that also accelerated
the process of collaboration.

00:38:51.610 --> 00:38:53.860
It accelerated the process
of how do we work together,

00:38:53.860 --> 00:38:55.500
why are working together?

00:38:55.500 --> 00:38:58.240
And what is the importance
of going offline and online?

00:38:58.240 --> 00:39:01.840
We needed to
straddle both spaces

00:39:01.840 --> 00:39:06.040
with equal forms of engagement,
equal level of engagement.

00:39:06.040 --> 00:39:08.320
And the same intensity
and complexity.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:10.260
So it's something which--

00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:13.557
I agree with Chucho in the sense
that the class has shifted.

00:39:13.557 --> 00:39:15.640
I think the turning point
for the classes shifting

00:39:15.640 --> 00:39:18.470
was when Trump made that
announcement and then

00:39:18.470 --> 00:39:19.720
suddenly everyone's panicking.

00:39:19.720 --> 00:39:25.350
But that once that sort
of went off the table,

00:39:25.350 --> 00:39:29.890
the idea of trying
to go offline did not

00:39:29.890 --> 00:39:32.350
go off the table, which
was something very good.

00:39:32.350 --> 00:39:37.270
And I mean, in many
ways, it's worked

00:39:37.270 --> 00:39:40.930
for the better for a lot of us.

00:39:40.930 --> 00:39:45.460
Of course, there are, I mean
shop access, I mean equipment,

00:39:45.460 --> 00:39:47.390
these things are
always a problem.

00:39:47.390 --> 00:39:51.080
But you have to negotiate
that on a one to one basis.

00:39:51.080 --> 00:39:55.050
But in terms of
interaction, to be honest,

00:39:55.050 --> 00:39:57.870
I think it brought us a
lot closer with each other.

00:39:57.870 --> 00:40:00.060
Because at some
point, we realized

00:40:00.060 --> 00:40:02.940
we have to create a community
in a completely different space

00:40:02.940 --> 00:40:04.840
all together now.

00:40:04.840 --> 00:40:07.804
So different things
are at stake.

00:40:07.804 --> 00:40:08.680
Great.

