00:41:36.890 --> 00:41:39.740
Cutting Across the
Archive, From Photo Montage

00:41:39.740 --> 00:41:40.940
to Digital Folklore.

00:41:40.940 --> 00:41:42.680
This Advanced
Photography course is

00:41:42.680 --> 00:41:45.710
designed for students who wish
to explore photography, images,

00:41:45.710 --> 00:41:48.080
and archives as
tools and resources

00:41:48.080 --> 00:41:49.370
for artistic practices.

00:41:49.370 --> 00:41:51.860
The course focuses on the
use of archival images

00:41:51.860 --> 00:41:54.380
and photographic practices
while encouraging students

00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:59.050
to explore analog,
digital, and [AUDIO OUT]

00:41:59.050 --> 00:42:00.190
and new technologies.

00:42:00.190 --> 00:42:03.190
Through lectures, readings,
film screenings, student driven

00:42:03.190 --> 00:42:05.110
projects, visiting
artist presentations,

00:42:05.110 --> 00:42:06.880
and critic sessions,
students experiment

00:42:06.880 --> 00:42:08.500
with a range of
artistic strategies

00:42:08.500 --> 00:42:10.660
while engaging in cross
disciplinary research

00:42:10.660 --> 00:42:13.180
and working in collaborative
and individual assignments.

00:42:13.180 --> 00:42:16.130
Across a diverse spectrum of
themes and historical context,

00:42:16.130 --> 00:42:18.370
students read and
discuss theoretical texts

00:42:18.370 --> 00:42:21.130
related to the use of archives
and artistic practices.

