Advanced Video
and Related Media.

00:42:32.640 --> 00:42:35.550
This course introduces advanced
strategies of image and sound

00:42:35.550 --> 00:42:38.680
manipulation, both
technical and conceptual.

00:42:38.680 --> 00:42:41.190
We'll cover everything from
preproduction planning,

00:42:41.190 --> 00:42:43.050
storyboards, and
scripting through

00:42:43.050 --> 00:42:45.480
the refinement of digital
editing techniques,

00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:48.660
visual effects such as
Chroma Key, post-production,

00:42:48.660 --> 00:42:51.690
as well as audio and
sonic components.

00:42:51.690 --> 00:42:54.810
Context is provided by regular
viewings of contemporary video

00:42:54.810 --> 00:42:56.835
artworks and other
audio visual formats.

00:43:01.480 --> 00:43:04.240
Video Installation is a
contemporary and expanding art

00:43:04.240 --> 00:43:06.550
genre that intersects with
the world of architecture,

00:43:06.550 --> 00:43:09.250
engineering, programming,
new media, and performance

00:43:09.250 --> 00:43:09.970
practices.

00:43:09.970 --> 00:43:11.800
In this intermediate
to advanced course,

00:43:11.800 --> 00:43:14.320
students are encouraged to
expand the current themes

00:43:14.320 --> 00:43:16.810
and methods within their
art or research practices

00:43:16.810 --> 00:43:19.150
by experimenting with
various video installation

00:43:19.150 --> 00:43:22.730
strategies, such as video
mapping to 3D objects, site

00:43:22.730 --> 00:43:25.720
specific architectural projects,
multi-channel projection

00:43:25.720 --> 00:43:27.610
environments,
mixing moving image

00:43:27.610 --> 00:43:30.100
content with live performance,
wearable sculptures,

00:43:30.100 --> 00:43:33.880
live feeds, physical computing,
or other elements of interest.

00:43:33.880 --> 00:43:36.930
